     <article class="story single" data-beat="positive">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">POSITIVE</span> · The Better India · 2026-09-28 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>6 Things ASHA Workers Want Every Household To Know About Dengue And Malaria Prevention</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Health</span> <span>#Public Health</span> <span>#Dengue</span> <span>#Malaria</span></div>
       <p>India's ASHA workers are on the frontline, tirelessly educating communities to prevent dengue and malaria, especially during monsoon. They dispel crucial myths, starting with the fact that dengue-carrying Aedes aegypti mosquitoes prefer clean, still water found in household items like overhead tanks and flowerpot trays, not just dirty water. This often-overlooked detail is critical for effective prevention.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-28/6-things-asha-workers-want-every-household-to-know-about-den.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>ASHA workers explain that municipal fogging only kills adult mosquitoes, leaving larvae and eggs to hatch again, making it a temporary solution. They stress that dengue and malaria require distinct treatments; rapid diagnostic tests are essential, as dengue's critical phase often begins after the fever subsides. They also caution against unproven home remedies, which can delay vital hospital care.</p><p>Crucially, ASHA workers emphasize that prevention is a shared responsibility. Residents must actively drain stagnant water, cover containers, and clear waste around their homes. These dedicated efforts, often undervalued, are pivotal in preventing outbreaks, one torch-lit inspection at a time.</p><p>Why it matters: The tireless efforts of ASHA workers are vital in educating communities and preventing vector-borne diseases across India.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately summarizes the key points from the source text while maintaining a professional tone.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://thebetterindia.com/health-care/6-things-asha-workers-dengue-malaria-prevention-12575597" rel="noopener">The Better India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
