     <article class="story single" data-beat="positive">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">POSITIVE</span> · The Better India · 2026-09-28 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>After 7 Years of UPSC Heartbreak &amp; Burnout, 32-YO Found Her Purpose in 800+ Rural Kids</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#social work</span> <span>#education</span> <span>#women empowerment</span> <span>#inspiration</span></div>
       <p>In 2024, Shruti Shrivastava faced profound disappointment after seven years and six attempts at the UPSC Civil Services Examination, capturing her heartbreak on camera when her name was absent from the final list. This moment, following extensive preparation and an interview, left her questioning her worth and future.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-28/after-7-years-of-upsc-heartbreak-burnout-32-yo-found-her-pur.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>However, from this personal setback emerged a new, powerful purpose. Shruti transitioned from an aspirant to a leader, now heading the 'Sashaktikaran Foundation' in Bhopal. Through her work, she supports over 800 rural children, enhancing their access to education. Additionally, the foundation empowers approximately 30 women by helping them build sustainable livelihoods.</p><p>Shruti describes this journey as a process of grieving, healing, and ultimately learning that 'a dream can end without a life ending with it.' Her story exemplifies resilience, demonstrating how a redirected passion can create significant positive change, transforming personal challenges into impactful community service.</p><p>Why it matters: It shows how personal setbacks can lead to profound community impact and a redefined sense of purpose.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Consistent with the source narrative; all figures and quotes are supported.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://thebetterindia.com/changemakers/shruti-shrivastava-upsc-failure-mental-health-journey-therapy-setback-healing-finding-purpose-12583174" rel="noopener">The Better India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
