     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · Al Jazeera · 2026-09-28 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Ben-Gvir joins hundreds of Israelis to storm Al-Aqsa Mosque compound</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#World</span> <span>#Middle East</span> <span>#Israel</span> <span>#Palestine</span></div>
       <p>Israel's national security minister, Ben-Gvir, reportedly participated alongside hundreds of Israelis in an incursion into the sensitive Al-Aqsa Mosque compound. This event saw a substantial number of individuals enter the site, which was conducted under heavy security.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-28/ben-gvir-joins-hundreds-of-israelis-to-storm-al-aqsa-mosque-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>During the incursion, the Israeli national security minister made a provocative declaration, asserting, &quot;we are the owners of the place in Al-Aqsa.&quot; This statement, delivered within the highly contested compound, is expected to intensify existing tensions and draw significant international scrutiny regarding the status of the holy site. The Al-Aqsa Mosque compound remains a critical flashpoint for religious and political disputes in the region.</p><p>The involvement of a high-ranking government official in such an event lends considerable political weight to the action. Incursions into the compound, particularly when accompanied by declarations of ownership, have historically been met with strong reactions and often contribute to instability. The heavy security presence during the entry suggests a recognition of the potential for heightened sensitivities and security challenges surrounding the action.</p><p>What to watch: The immediate aftermath, including any official statements from regional and international bodies, and potential for further unrest.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Faithfully reflects source; no extraneous claims.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/9/28/ben-gvir-joins-hundreds-of-israelis-to-storm-al-aqsa-mosque-compound?traffic_source=rss" rel="noopener">Al Jazeera</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
