       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-09-28 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>India vs Afghanistan Quarterfinal Abandoned Due to Rain at Asian Games 2026</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Sports</span> <span>#Cricket</span> <span>#Asian Games 2026</span> <span>#India</span></div>
       <p>The men's cricket quarterfinal between India and Afghanistan at the Asian Games 2026 was abandoned without a toss due to heavy rain in Nisshin on Monday. The adverse weather conditions made it impossible to commence the match, leading to the immediate cancellation of the contest. This development has significant implications for the tournament's progression, as the abandonment of a quarterfinal affects the advancement of teams to the next stage.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-28/india-vs-afghanistan-quarterfinal-abandoned-due-to-rain-at-a.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The match was scheduled to be a crucial encounter in the quarterfinals, with both teams vying for a spot in the semifinals. The rain in Nisshin, where the matches are being held, has disrupted the schedule, causing delays and cancellations. The decision to abandon the match without a toss indicates that the conditions were deemed unfit for play from the outset. This is a rare occurrence in high-profile cricket matches, highlighting the impact of weather on sporting events.</p><p>The announcement of the abandonment has left fans and teams uncertain about the next steps in the tournament. The organizing committee has not yet clarified how the abandonment will affect the qualification of teams for the semifinals. Both India and Afghanistan will now await further instructions regarding the impact on their tournament journey. The incident underscores the challenges of hosting outdoor sports in variable weather conditions.</p><p>What to watch: The tournament committee's decision on which team qualifies for the semifinal following the abandoned match.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately summarizes the provided source without adding extraneous or unbacked information.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/cricket/india-vs-afghanistan-live-score-ind-vs-afg-asian-games-2026-quarterfinal-live-updates-aichi-nagoya-japan-shreyas-iyer-vaibhav-sooryavanshi-12107226#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
