       <h1>Julianne Moore to Receive Icon Award at SCAD Savannah Film Festival With ‘The Dead Donkey’ Set as Centerpiece Selection</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#film festival</span> <span>#award</span> <span>#Julianne Moore</span> <span>#A24</span></div>
       <p>The Savannah College of Art and Design announced that Julianne Moore will be honored with the Icon Award at this year’s SCAD Savannah Film Festival. The ceremony will also feature Moore’s film “The Dead Donkey,” a musical comedy starring Jesse Eisenberg and produced by A24, as the festival’s Centerpiece selection. The award recognizes Moore’s decades‑long contributions to cinema, and the Centerpiece slot highlights the collaborative project that pairs her with Eisenberg’s comedic sensibility. The festival’s opening program will include Bleecker Street’s “A Talent for …,” signaling a broader slate of high‑profile releases. Organizers said the combination of Moore’s accolade and the Centerpiece film underscores SCAD’s commitment to showcasing both established talent and emerging storytelling forms. Attendees can expect a series of screenings, panels, and networking events that celebrate the intersection of film artistry and academic engagement. </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-28/julianne-moore-to-receive-icon-award-at-scad-savannah-film-f.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>What to watch: The reception of “The Dead Donkey” as the Centerpiece may influence its awards trajectory and future distribution plans.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the source summary provided.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://variety.com/2026/film/news/the-debut-scad-centerpiece-julianne-moore-honor-1236877183/" rel="noopener">Variety</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
