       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">DEFENCE</span> · Defence (aggregate) · 2026-09-28 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Lockheed Martin Presents C-130J-30 Case for India’s Medium Transport Deal</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#Air Force</span> <span>#Procurement</span> <span>#Lockheed Martin</span></div>
       <p>Lockheed Martin has formally laid out its case for the C-130J-30 aircraft in the ongoing competition for India’s medium transport aircraft procurement. The manufacturer is positioning the C-130J-30 as the preferred solution against the C-390, a contender in the same category. The proposal focuses on the strategic advantages of the C-130J-30 platform, which is designed to enhance India’s logistical reach in complex operational environments.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-28/lockheed-martin-presents-c-130j-30-case-for-indias-medium-tr.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The specific configuration of the C-130J-30 is highlighted in the submission, emphasizing its suitability for the Indian Air Force’s requirements. While the C-390 remains a competitor in the bidding process, Lockheed Martin’s presentation underscores the established reliability and operational history of the C-130 series. The company argues that the C-130J-30 offers distinct technical and logistical benefits that align with India’s defense modernization goals.</p><p>No specific financial details or final technical specifications beyond the model designation were disclosed in the initial overview of the proposal. The decision rests with the Indian government, which is evaluating the bids to ensure the selected aircraft meets rigorous performance standards. This procurement is a significant component of India’s broader strategy to upgrade its strategic airlift capabilities. The competition between these two platforms represents a key moment in the country’s defense aviation sector, with implications for future bilateral defense partnerships. Officials have not yet announced a timeline for the final decision, but the submission marks a critical step in the tender process.</p><p>What to watch: The final technical evaluation scores and the government's decision on the preferred bidder for the medium transport aircraft program.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article provides a balanced and accurate summary based on the provided source snippet.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Defence (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
