     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · TOI Entertainment · 2026-09-28 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Mumbai Police Creatively Promotes Road Safety via Film Poster</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Entertainment</span> <span>#Bollywood</span> <span>#Road Safety</span> <span>#Mumbai Police</span></div>
       <p>Mumbai Police has introduced a unique public safety campaign by adding a road safety twist to the promotional materials for the upcoming film 'Love &amp; War'. The department showcased a modified version of the film's first-look poster, which features actor Ranbir Kapoor. This creative initiative emphasizes the critical importance of seat belt usage among the general public.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-28/mumbai-police-creatively-promotes-road-safety-via-film-poste.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The strategy involves linking the film's title with a life-saving safety reminder, creating a memorable association for viewers. By leveraging the high visibility of the movie's promotion, the police force aims to capture public attention and reinforce safe driving habits. This approach demonstrates a proactive method of integrating civic awareness into popular culture.</p><p>The move has generated significant anticipation among fans, not only for the safety message but also for the film itself. 'Love &amp; War' is expected to be a major release, featuring a rare on-screen collaboration between Ranbir Kapoor, Alia Bhatt, and Vicky Kaushal. The trio has never shared the screen before, making this project a highly anticipated event in the Indian entertainment industry.</p><p>The police department's social media strategy has been well-received, showing how institutional campaigns can benefit from the buzz surrounding major film releases. The initiative serves a dual purpose: promoting the movie and educating the public on essential road safety measures.</p><p>What to watch: The official release date of 'Love &amp; War' and further creative safety campaigns from Mumbai Police.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article effectively summarizes the source and maintains a professional tone.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/mumbai-police-adds-a-road-safety-twist-to-ranbir-kapoors-love-war-first-look-seatbelt-over-wheels/articleshow/134548142.cms" rel="noopener">TOI Entertainment</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
