       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">DEFENCE</span> · Defence (aggregate) · 2026-09-28 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Navy Chief Directs Skyroot to Develop Next-Gen Space Defence Capabilities</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#Space</span> <span>#Indian Navy</span> <span>#Skyroot</span></div>
       <p>The Chief of the Naval Staff has engaged with Skyroot, a prominent Indian private space company, to accelerate the development of next-generation space defence capabilities. The directive emphasizes the need for indigenous solutions to bolster India’s strategic posture in the space domain. This collaboration signals a growing integration between the Indian Navy’s operational requirements and the private sector’s technological advancements in aerospace.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-28/navy-chief-directs-skyroot-to-develop-next-gen-space-defence.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The focus is on building robust capabilities that address emerging threats in space, which are increasingly viewed as critical to national security. Skyroot is tasked with contributing to these efforts, leveraging its expertise in launch vehicle technology and space systems. The Navy’s involvement highlights the expanding role of space assets in naval operations and broader defense strategies. This move aligns with India’s broader defense modernization agenda, which prioritizes indigenous manufacturing and technological self-reliance.</p><p>No specific technical details or project timelines were disclosed in the initial reports of this engagement. The initiative represents a significant step in the partnership between military institutions and private entities in the space sector. By directing Skyroot to build these capabilities, the Navy aims to ensure that India maintains a competitive edge in space-based defence technologies. The collaboration is expected to foster innovation and reduce dependency on foreign suppliers for critical space defence systems. This strategic alignment underscores the importance of space in contemporary warfare and national security frameworks.</p><p>What to watch: The specific technological milestones and contractual agreements between the Indian Navy and Skyroot for space defence projects.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the source's core message regarding the Navy Chief's engagement with Skyroot.</p>
