       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-09-28 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Nepal Mountain Crashes Into Kali Gandaki River: Should India Be Worried Amid Landslide, Cliff Collapse &amp; Avalanche?</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#National</span> <span>#Nepal</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#Disaster</span></div>
       <p>A recent incident has seen a mountain in Nepal crash into the Kali Gandaki River, prompting concerns about regional stability. This event contributes to an ongoing sense of unease, with questions being raised about whether the worst of Nepal's natural disasters might still be unfolding.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-28/nepal-mountain-crashes-into-kali-gandaki-river-should-india-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This latest disruption follows a significant glacier and rock collapse in August, an earlier catastrophe that tragically claimed over 1,300 lives. The scale of the previous event highlights the severe geological vulnerabilities in the region and the potential for widespread impact from such natural occurrences. The current situation, involving a mountain collapsing into a major river, suggests a continuation of these environmental challenges.</p><p>In response to these developments and the potential for cascading effects, 17 districts in the Indian state of Bihar have been placed on high alert. This precautionary measure underscores the seriousness with which Indian authorities are viewing the situation, preparing for any possible repercussions from the ongoing geological events in Nepal, including the threats of landslides, cliff collapses, and avalanches in vulnerable areas.</p><p>What to watch: Authorities in Bihar will continue to monitor the situation closely for any further developments.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately reflects the source points regarding Nepal and Bihar districts.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/explainers/nepal-mountain-crashes-into-kali-gandaki-river-worst-not-over-yet-should-india-be-worried-ws-klrt-10357767.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
