       <h1>NIA court sentences 4 ISIS operatives in 'Voice of Hind' terror conspiracy case</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#National Security</span> <span>#NIA</span> <span>#Terrorism</span> <span>#Legal</span></div>
       <p>An NIA court has delivered sentences to four individuals identified as operatives of the global terror group ISIS, in connection with the 'Voice of Hind' terror conspiracy case. The judicial proceedings culminated in the sentencing of these four operatives, marking a significant development in ongoing national security efforts against extremist networks.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-28/nia-court-sentences-4-isis-operatives-in-voice-of-hind-terro.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The case revolves around the 'Voice of Hind' conspiracy, an alleged plot involving the propagation of extremist ideology and activities linked to ISIS. The National Investigation Agency (NIA) has been at the forefront of investigating such cases, aiming to dismantle modules and prevent terror-related acts within the country. The court's decision to sentence the four operatives underscores the gravity of the charges and the judicial system's response to threats posed by international terror organizations. While specific details regarding the nature of their involvement or the duration of their sentences were not provided in the summary, the outcome reflects the culmination of investigative and legal processes dedicated to counter-terrorism. This judgment serves as a deterrent against individuals attempting to align with or support terror outfits operating on national soil.</p><p>What to watch: Further details on the sentences and ongoing investigations into terror networks.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reports the sentencing of the four operatives based on the source provided.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/story/isis-voice-of-hind-delhi-nia-court-sentences-four-operatives-up-to-six-years-terror-conspiracy-case-3005250-2026-09-28?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
