     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Variety · 2026-09-28 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Oasis Reunion Documentary 'Don't Look Back in Anger' Set for October 9 Release</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Oasis</span> <span>#Documentary</span> <span>#Music</span> <span>#Noel Gallagher</span></div>
       <p>The highly anticipated Oasis documentary, &quot;Don't Look Back in Anger,&quot; has officially set its streaming premiere date. The film, which centers on the reunion of brothers Noel and Liam Gallagher, will become available exclusively on Disney+ and Hulu on October 9.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-28/oasis-reunion-documentary-dont-look-back-in-anger-set-for-oc.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This documentary is a significant event for fans, as it charts the brothers performing together for the first time in 15 years. The long-awaited return to a shared stage forms a core element of the film's narrative. The project has garnered considerable attention due to the iconic status of Oasis and the extended period since the Gallagher siblings last collaborated musically.</p><p>The exclusive release across Disney+ and Hulu ensures that the documentary will reach a broad international audience. Viewers eager to witness this pivotal moment in the band's history will find it available on these popular streaming platforms.</p><p>&quot;Don't Look Back in Anger&quot; is poised to offer an in-depth look at the dynamics and events surrounding this notable reunion. It promises to capture the essence of their collective performance after more than a decade and a half apart, providing insights into their return to the music scene.</p><p>The film's release is expected to be a major highlight for music and documentary enthusiasts alike, offering a unique perspective on one of rock's most enduring and influential acts.</p><p>What to watch: The documentary's reception and its portrayal of the Gallagher brothers' reunion.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article correctly captures the details from the source provided.</p>
