     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-09-28 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Sharad Pawar Refutes Merger Speculations, Vows Independence</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Politics</span> <span>#Sharad Pawar</span> <span>#NDA</span> <span>#Indian Politics</span></div>
       <p>Veteran leader Sharad Pawar has firmly put a stop to ongoing speculation regarding a potential merger for his political party. Addressing the rumors directly, Pawar stated that he will not join any other political entity, effectively ending the debate on his party's alignment with existing coalitions.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-28/sharad-pawar-refutes-merger-speculations-vows-independence.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The speculation had intensified in recent days following reports that Pawar met with Prime Minister Narendra Modi. This meeting fueled widespread conjecture about whether his party would shift its support to the ruling National Democratic Alliance (NDA). However, Pawar’s recent remarks clarify that no such alliance is being formed at the leadership level.</p><p>Despite his refusal to merge or join another party, Pawar indicated a degree of openness regarding future interactions. He noted that while his own political path remains independent, his doors remain open to others who may wish to engage in dialogue or collaboration on specific issues. This stance suggests a strategy of maintaining autonomy while keeping communication lines open with other political stakeholders.</p><p>The clarification comes at a critical juncture for the political landscape, where coalition dynamics are often closely scrutinized. By explicitly denying the merger rumors, Pawar aims to stabilize his party's identity and reassure its base that its independent trajectory remains unchanged.</p><p>What to watch: Future public interactions between Pawar and other party leaders to gauge the substance of his 'open doors' remark.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the source material without adding extraneous claims.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/maharashtra/sharad-pawar-puts-a-stop-to-merger-speculation-says-he-wont-join-anyone/article71520898.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
