     <article class="story single" data-beat="tech">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · TechCrunch · 2026-09-28 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Shopify Integrates AI Agents into Checkout Process</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Shopify</span> <span>#AI</span> <span>#E-commerce</span> <span>#Technology</span></div>
       <p>Shopify has announced a significant expansion of its WebMCP support, now extending its capabilities to the checkout process. This development will enable browser-based AI agents to interact directly with the checkout flow, streamlining online purchases. The integration aims to enhance the e-commerce experience by automating certain aspects of transaction completion.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-28/shopify-integrates-ai-agents-into-checkout-process.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The new functionality allows these AI agents to perform critical tasks such as updating order details. Crucially, any action taken by an AI agent to complete purchases will require explicit authorization from the buyer. This ensures that while the process is automated, human oversight and consent remain central to the transaction.</p><p>This move by Shopify reflects a broader trend in e-commerce towards leveraging artificial intelligence to improve efficiency and user experience. By opening its checkout to AI agents, Shopify is positioning its platform to adapt to evolving digital shopping habits and technologies. Merchants on the Shopify platform may see benefits in reduced friction during checkout, potentially leading to higher conversion rates as the process becomes more seamless for authorized AI-assisted buyers.</p><p>What to watch: The impact of AI agents on e-commerce conversion rates and buyer experience.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately describes the expansion of WebMCP support to Shopify's checkout.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/09/28/shopify-opens-checkout-to-browser-based-ai-agents/" rel="noopener">TechCrunch</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-09-28/shopify-integrates-ai-agents-into-checkout-process" data-title="Shopify Integrates AI Agents into Checkout Process"><b>Share:</b>
         <a class="sh-wa" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="ic" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8 1.8A6.2 6.2 0 0 0 2.7 11L1.8 14.2l3.3-.9A6.2 6.2 0 1 0 8 1.8z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>WhatsApp</a> ·
