       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-09-28 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>SP Chief To Skip INDIA Bloc Meet, Seat-Sharing Rift With Congress And Opposition Strategy Over CEC</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#SP Chief</span> <span>#INDIA Bloc</span> <span>#Congress</span> <span>#Seat-Sharing</span></div>
       <p>The Chief of the Samajwadi Party (SP) is set to skip the upcoming meeting of the INDIA Bloc, a significant development that underscores existing internal challenges within the opposition alliance. This decision comes amidst reports of a growing seat-sharing rift between the SP and the Congress party, a key component of the INDIA Bloc.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-28/sp-chief-to-skip-india-bloc-meet-seat-sharing-rift-with-cong.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The absence of a prominent leader from a crucial ally at such a gathering signals potential hurdles in forging a united front ahead of future electoral contests. Seat-sharing negotiations are often a contentious aspect of multi-party alliances, as each party seeks to maximize its electoral prospects. Disagreements on this front can significantly impact the cohesion and effectiveness of a coalition.</p><p>Furthermore, the meeting was also slated to address the opposition's strategy concerning the Chief Election Commissioner (CEC). The formulation of a unified approach on such critical institutional matters is vital for the alliance's overall political agenda. The SP Chief's decision to abstain from these discussions highlights the complexities and differing viewpoints that may be present among the constituent parties.</p><p>What to watch: How the INDIA Bloc addresses the absence and works to resolve internal differences.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article effectively expands on the source summary while remaining strictly within the factual boundaries provided.</p>
