     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-09-28 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Violent Protests Erupt at LPU Over Alleged Assault Claim, SIT Ordered</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#LPU</span> <span>#Student Protest</span> <span>#Phagwara</span> <span>#Punjab</span></div>
       <p>Tensions have significantly escalated at Lovely Professional University (LPU) in Phagwara, Punjab, following student protests over an alleged sexual assault claim involving a female student. The demonstration reportedly drew around 2,000 students and turned violent, leading to damage to university property, fires, and a blockade of the Jalandhar-Phagwara stretch of National Highway-44.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-28/violent-protests-erupt-at-lpu-over-alleged-assault-claim-sit.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>During the clashes, several police personnel sustained injuries, and multiple vehicles were damaged. Authorities have since registered an FIR against an unidentified individual and constituted a Special Investigation Team (SIT) to probe the allegation, which includes examining CCTV footage and other pertinent evidence.</p><p>The university, however, has denied the alleged sexual assault, labeling the claims circulating on social media as false and fabricated. Meanwhile, Punjab Chief Minister Bhagwant Mann has directed the state police leadership to investigate the situation thoroughly. In response to the unrest, LPU has suspended regular classes for a period of ten days and postponed mid-term examinations. The situation remains under close scrutiny as the investigation proceeds.</p><p>What to watch: The findings of the Special Investigation Team and the university's response to the allegations.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article provides a faithful and comprehensive summary of the source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/videos/india/lpu-university-campus-news-2-000-students-protest-alleged-assault-sit-probe-ordered-punjab-news-10356490.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
