      <a href="/feed.xml" title="RSS">RSS</a>
      <button id="tdp-theme" title="Toggle light/dark">Light</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <nav class="catrow"><span class="catgrp"><b>News</b><a href="/category/national">national</a><a href="/category/world">world</a><a href="/category/defence">defence</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Money</b><a href="/category/business">business</a><a href="/category/finance">finance</a><a href="/category/education">education</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Sports</b><a href="/category/sports">sports</a><a href="/category/cricket">cricket</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Culture</b><a href="/category/entertainment">entertainment</a><a href="/category/positive">positive</a><a href="/category/funny">funny</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Life</b><a href="/category/science">science</a><a href="/category/environment">environment</a><a href="/category/space">space</a><a href="/category/health">health</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Tech</b><a href="/category/tech">tech</a><a href="/category/ai">ai</a></span></nav></div><div class="gtr"><span>Read in your language:</span><div id="google_translate_element"></div></div><div class="wrap"><main id="content"><p class="crumb"><a href="/">← Front page</a> · <a href="/archive">Archive</a> · <a href="/category/space">space</a></p>
     <article class="story single" data-beat="space">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPACE</span> · NASA · 2026-09-28 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>What You Need to Know About NASA’s SpaceX Crew-13 Mission</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#NASA</span> <span>#SpaceX</span> <span>#International Space Station</span> <span>#Space Mission</span></div>
       <p>NASA and SpaceX are preparing for the upcoming Crew-13 mission, which will see four astronauts launch to the International Space Station (ISS). This collaborative effort underscores the ongoing partnership between the national space agency and commercial spaceflight provider in advancing human space exploration. The primary objective of the Crew-13 mission is to transport its four-member crew to the orbiting laboratory, where they will embark on a comprehensive program of scientific inquiry and operational duties.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-09-28/what-you-need-to-know-about-nasas-spacex-crew-13-mission.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Upon arrival at the International Space Station, the crew members are slated to engage in a diverse array of activities. These include conducting vital research experiments across various disciplines, pushing the boundaries of scientific understanding in microgravity. Additionally, the mission will focus on critical technology demonstrations, testing new systems and equipment that are essential for future long-duration space travel and deeper space exploration initiatives. The crew will also be responsible for performing routine maintenance tasks, ensuring the continued optimal operation and habitability of the International Space Station, a crucial outpost for international cooperation and scientific advancement. The launch of the Crew-13 mission represents another significant step in maintaining a continuous human presence in low-Earth orbit.</p><p>What to watch: Details on the specific launch window and crew profiles are anticipated.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately summarizes the source information without adding unverified claims.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.nasa.gov/missions/station/commercial-crew/what-you-need-to-know-about-nasas-spacex-crew-13-mission/" rel="noopener">NASA</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
